# What: Sample HTTP requests for the remote-bp sample (VS Code "REST Client" / IntelliJ HTTP client).
# Why: [CAP-M08] click through delegation and replication without writing code.
# If missing or unlinked: Learners have to reconstruct the URLs from the tests.
#
# Start first: npm run watch (mocks API_BUSINESS_PARTNER from srv/external/data).

@P = http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/partners

### 1 Live: blocked partners, filtered in the remote API
GET {{P}}/RemotePartners?$filter=blocked eq true&$select=name,lastChanged

### 2 Replicated copy before the load (2 rows from db/data)
GET {{P}}/Partners

### 3 Full replication: 4 created, 1 updated (Kanto is blocked now), 1 unchanged
POST {{P}}/replicateAll
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 4 Again - everything unchanged (idempotent)
POST {{P}}/replicateAll
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 5 Local data supports what the remote API cannot do cheaply: sort and filter at will
GET {{P}}/Partners?$filter=country eq 'DE' or blocked eq true&$orderby=name
